            <ArticleTitle>MRI of impingement syndromes of the shoulder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.crad.2008.08.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis of shoulder impingement is primarily a clinical one. Imaging has a role in assisting clinicians in developing a treatment strategy by identifying and characterizing the cause of shoulder impingement. In this review, the relevant anatomy, cause/pathomechanics, clinical features, and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) findings of the different types of impingement syndromes are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
